Z||000000||Alex2004||11-24-2001||11:52 PM||||On my 84 i notice sometimes whenever i'm driving harder than normal sometimes when the rpms are about 3.5-4 it will kinda flicker or just barly come on and then earlier tonight i was trying to get my friend home and we were at about 95-100 mph and it was coming on also. then when i got to her house, whenever i put it in reverse it came on and didn't go off till i shut the car off.  Why does this come on?  And what do i need to replace.  Thanks<P>Alex...||||reg||4
Z||000001||maryjane||11-25-2001||12:50 AM||||I'm guessing it is a 4cyl since it's an 84. How many miles on the eng? Had the valve cover off lately? It can be a sensor or wiring problem, even in the light itself..if your lucky. Could be foaming in the oil at high rpms(not likely, if you are doing good maint). If it is a high mileage eng, the top of the cyl head may be sludged/carboned up, the oil isn't able to drain back to the pan quickly enough to be picked up by the pump.<BR>Some of the early '84 engines had the wrong<BR>dipstick and called for 3 instead of 4 qts of oil. Supposed to be corrected with one of the first recalls.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||11-25-2001||09:53 AM||||Changed the oil latey??||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex2004||11-25-2001||05:41 PM||||It has 96,7** on it, i haven't had the valve cover off in a while, last time was when my dad was doing something to my engine.  I changed the oil about 1K or less ago, and it's been leaking oil but i cannot figure out from where yet.  So i've been topping it off a lot lately.  It read what it was supposed to on the dipstick.  And when i changed the oil i did use 4 quarts.  Hope that helps.  <BR>Alex..||||reg||2
Z||000004||Alex2004||11-25-2001||05:47 PM||||Ok, once i checked the oil right after i shut it off and there was little bubles on the dipstick.  What would cause oil to foam?  I'm going to replace my engine as soon as i get enough money anyways, but that'll be a while.  I try to maintain my engine pretty well.  my check engine light as never came on except when one of my sensors came loose.  Thanks...<BR>Alex...<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR>[B]Could be foaming in the oil at high rpms(not likely, if you are doing good maint). B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><p>[This message has been edited by Alex2004 (edited 11-25-2001).]||||reg||1
